---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Container from '@brandcloud/astro/components/Container.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy and contact" description="How BrandCloud handles free tool inputs and requests for a Pro launch email.">
 <Container><header class="s-pagehead"><h1>Privacy and contact</h1><p class="s-lead">The free tools work without an account. A Pro launch request is a separate choice.</p></header>
 <section class="s-stack"><h2>Your brand files and page checks</h2><p>The brand builder and AI-look score process your input in your browser. Your uploaded logo and pasted HTML are not submitted with a launch request. Download your results to keep them.</p>
 <h2>A Pro launch request</h2><p>If you choose the launch email, we use your email address, optional first name and permission record to manage that request. The record includes the page, time and wording of your consent. It does not create a Brand CRM workspace or subscribe you to other marketing.</p>
 <p>You can withdraw your request or ask about access, correction or deletion through <a href="https://m1studio.co.uk/contact/">M1 Studio contact</a>. Please say that your request is about BrandCloud. Do not include passwords or licence tokens.</p>
 <h2>Who to contact</h2><p>BrandCloud is provided by Samuel Morgan, trading as M1 Studio. <a href="https://m1studio.co.uk/privacy/">M1 Studio's privacy notice</a> explains the wider handling of personal information and your rights.</p>
 <h2>Existing customer accounts</h2><p>Brand CRM is a separate signed-in application. <a href="https://brandui.cloud/app/">Existing customers can sign in here</a>. You do not need that account to use BrandCloud's free tools.</p></section>
 </Container>
</Base>
